title: "Virtual Power Plant Platform"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2025-02-24
url: "https://github.com/vinerya/virtual-power-plant"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vinerya/virtual-power-plant"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - virtual power plant
  - distributed energy resources
  - energy management
  - demand response
  - vehicle-to-grid
  - OCPP
  - OpenADR
  - IEEE 2030.5
  - optimization
  - smart grid
  - energy storage
abstract: |
  An open-source platform for aggregating and dispatching distributed
  energy resources. It provides a FastAPI backend with database-backed
  resource, site and customer management, dispatch optimization (Pyomo and
  HiGHS with rule-based fallbacks), model predictive control and
  backtesting, a URDB-based tariff and net-metering bill engine, an OCPP 1.6-J
  central system, an OpenADR 2.0b VEN, an IEEE 2030.5 client, a
  demand-response orchestrator, V2G scheduling, a trading engine on a
  simulated venue, and a Next.js operator console with a customer portal.
